Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:26:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] 034 B2 r2 (TKOffset): proven vanishing test, stock cap
 sections kept and prolonged across the set

Review B2 r1 findings 2-5:
- A rim face with an edge on a removed face keeps the stock section there
  (its non-vanishing end is shared with a tube, a surviving blend or
  another removed face); only the vanishing end is prolonged by the reach
  of the set (ToContext). Rim faces that reach the removed face only
  across the set keep the enlarged-copy pairs. Sections of two rim faces
  across a sharp edge are prolonged the same way when their set reaches a
  removed face (ConnexIntByArc hook), so a second removed face or a
  removed face tangent to the set is met beyond the stock end.
- The vanishing decision is proven: one-point refutation, canonical twin
  within the face tolerance (analytic rule of BRepOffset::Surface), else
  interval bounds per Bezier patch (hodograph hulls, Leibniz rule,
  trace/determinant of sigma*I - d*W); a face that is not proven is kept.
- Every interval of a rim edge is checked, not only the first.
- Rim offset boxes are computed once per face; VanishRecord034b::Caps
  (never read) replaced by RimMargin / SetVertices.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
